From 4262440b6ec87b1ebe9fe23737b567986b8b6d77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy Lyons <guylyons2@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 19:49:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] macos-arm64: ray-traced lighting layer (Metal)

- rtmetal: Metal ray tracing module (BVH of world geometry, AO and sun
  shadow rays, temporal accumulation, depth-aware blur, composite kernel).
- togl glmrt: depth resolve into an IOSurface-backed texture and a GLSL
  multiply composite, exported to the tracer via dlsym.
- stdshaders RayTraceComposite: shader whose draw pass runs the tracer on
  the render thread; matrices/settings travel as material vars.
- client rt_layer: BSP world geometry extraction (faces + displacements),
  light_environment sun direction, rt_* convars, capture and composite draws.
